AgentForge PostgreSQL migrations (v0.11+).

Connection: env.py reads DATABASE_URL from backend.core.config.settings
(sourced from the repo-root .env), or ALEMBIC_DATABASE_URL if set --
used to point the same migration set at a different database, e.g. the
test database, without editing alembic.ini.

Models: backend/db/models/ (Base.metadata is imported directly by
env.py for autogenerate; no model is registered anywhere else).

Common commands, run from the repository root:

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "<description>"
    alembic upgrade head
    alembic downgrade -1

    # apply the same migration set to a different database
    ALEMBIC_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://user:pass@host/db alembic upgrade head

See docs/Database_Design.md for the full schema and how DatabaseSyncService
keeps these tables in sync with workflow execution.